{"id": "unknown-2026-09-28-004", "date": "2026-09-28", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 40, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "MEG loses momentum as textile chain demand stays subdued", "content": "Global MEG prices retreated in the week to September 18, 2026, ending a four-week climb as sluggish polyester and textile demand weighed.\nMEG CFR India fell 5.5 per cent to $0.744 per kg; Southeast Asia dropped 5.8 per cent to $0.784 per kg on the week.\nDomestic China slipped 0.9 per cent to $1.046 per kg but stayed 18.1 per cent above late August, while FD NW Europe eased to 0.859.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/meg-loses-momentum-as-textile-chain-demand-stays-subdued-313822-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-28-005", "date": "2026-09-28", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 40, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Performance Days CEO to debut on fossil-free performance panel", "content": "Performance Days will expand its Munich education programme on October 13–14, 2026, covering bio-based materials, PFAS alternatives, circularity and EU rules.\nFor the first time, chief executive officer Marco Weichert will join an expert panel to discuss the road towards fossil-free performance.\nNew education formats will connect textile sourcing with practical innovation and compliance guidance.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/performance-days-ceo-to-debut-on-fossil-free-performance-panel-313819-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-28-006", "date": "2026-09-28", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 40, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.25, "keywords": ["[否定]loss", "pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India’s weavers seek six-month duty relief as yarn costs rise", "content": "Indian weaving representatives have urged the finance ministry to remove basic customs duty on MEG, PTA, POY, FDY and DTY for 6 months to ease polyester input costs.\nThe call follows price rises: PTA to ₹106.50 (~$1.11) per kg, polyester melt to ₹120.05 per kg and polyester staple fibre up ₹2 per kg from September 26.\nIndustry comments warned pressure could affect employment but did not quantify job losses.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-s-weavers-seek-six-month-duty-relief-as-yarn-costs-rise-313811-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-28-007", "date": "2026-09-28", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 40, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -1.0, "keywords": ["decline"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "China PFY falls and Pakistan rises: Why are Asia markets diverging?", "content": "China’s PFY ex-mill grades declined across the tracked range in the week ended September 25, with FDY 100D/72F down 3.03 per cent.\nIndia’s DTY 150D/48F held at ₹157.50/kg (~$1.64/kg), while Pakistan’s POY and DTY rose 1.75 per cent and 1.20 per cent.\nTexPro data point to divergent pricing conditions across China, India and Pakistan, shaped by demand, duties and input costs.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/china-pfy-falls-and-pakistan-rises-why-are-asia-markets-diverging--313817-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-28-008", "date": "2026-09-28", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 40, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["increase"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India’s PSF prices rise as domestic PTA, melt costs increase", "content": "Indian PSF prices increased by ₹2 (~$0.02) per kg from September 26, after a ₹3 per kg rise on September 16.\nDomestic PTA rose to ₹106.50 per kg and polyester melt to ₹120.05, while MEG stayed at ₹83.70.\nThe revisions lifted 1.4 denier PSF to ₹146 per kg, with cumulative gains of ₹5 per kg; CFR China PTA ended $40 per tonne above September 18.\nNo new filament yarn revision was indicated.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-s-psf-prices-rise-as-domestic-pta-melt-costs-increase-313810-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-28-009", "date": "2026-09-28", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 40, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth", "increase"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "China’s industrial profits rose 15.7% in first eight months of 2026", "content": "China’s industrial profits rose 15.7 per cent year on year to 5.27 trillion yuan in the first eight months of 2026, driven by strong gains in manufacturing and high-tech industries. \nManufacturing profits rose 17.4 per cent year on year to nearly 3.97 trillion yuan, while August industrial profits increased 4.2 per cent, extending the double-digit growth trend.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/china-s-industrial-profits-rose-15-7-in-first-eight-months-of-2026-313807-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-28-010", "date": "2026-09-28", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 40, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "India apparel’s next growth test: Can scale translate into profit?", "content": "India’s domestic apparel market is shifting from revenue growth towards profitability, retention, productivity and capital discipline.\nDaMENSCH raised ₹17.40 crore (~$1.81 million) from A91 Partners and Tancom Electronics at a broadly flat valuation of about ₹600 crore in early September 2026.\nABFRL reshaped Pantaloons, re-entering Nagaland as its national store count edged down.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/india-apparel-s-next-growth-test-can-scale-translate-into-profit--313816-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-28-011", "date": "2026-09-28", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 40, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 1.0, "keywords": ["record"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "$28 bn in apparel, $2.6 mn detained: Can US customs track the cotton?", "content": "TexPro records $27.30 billion of HS61–62 apparel exports from Vietnam to the US in November 2024–June 2026, close to a $28 billion estimate.\nVietnam imported $2.355 billion of US raw cotton, but China supplied $2.589 billion of cotton yarn and woven cotton fabric.\nUFLPA can follow upstream inputs across borders; proving fibre origin inside a finished garment remains harder.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/-28-bn-in-apparel-2-6-mn-detained-can-us-customs-track-the-cotton--313814-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-28-012", "date": "2026-09-28", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 40, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "BGMEA opens Japan Desk to boost Bangladesh's apparel exports", "content": "BGMEA has launched a Japan Desk in Dhaka to link Bangladeshi garment factories with Japanese buyers and support market diversification.\nAround 100 factories have been selected for buyer-supplier matchmaking, market information and issue resolution.\nThe association targets apparel exports to Japan of $3 billion by 2030, up from about $1.4 billion.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/bgmea-opens-japan-desk-to-boost-bangladesh-s-apparel-exports-313798-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
